{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":2,"timestamp":1784152915,"nonce":"mF66wafhNGywYujeF9Zniv9aUOU=","title":"[bug] Environment allowed-refs checked against commit SHA, not branch ref (no-op for push/PR/dispatch)","was":"Environment `allowed_refs` protection (ADR-0037) is checked against `config_ref(event)`, which returns the **commit SHA** for Push/PullRequest/Manual/Api events (GitHub's `after`/`head`; a dispatch's resolved SHA), not the branch ref. `ProtectionRules::ref_allowed` glob-matches that value, so a branch-pattern rule (e.g. `refs/heads/main` or `main`) can **never** match a SHA — allowed-refs is effectively a no-op for these event kinds (only Tag/Release feed a `refs/tags/*` string)."}]}